  ('p-vpod-elite-single', 'VPod Postpartum & Menopause Comfort Single Pack', 'VPod', 'postpartum', 'physical', 'VPod’s extra-soft cooling gel pod designed for new moms, for targeted relief of tearing, bruising, swelling, dryness, and irritation before and after birth, and for menopause-related discomfort. Like the Everyday pod, you freeze it and place it in your underwear for up to 20 minutes; it has a 100% medical-grade silicone exterior and is drug-free. It eases symptoms but doesn’t treat their cause. One pod per pack; sold as VPod Elite.', '$21.99 (1 pod)', '/products/vpod/elite-single.webp', 'https://hervpod.com/products/vpod-elite-single-pack', '["discomfort","comfort","postpartum","pregnancy","menopause","external-only","reusable","hormone-free"]'::jsonb, '["vaginal-health","comfort"]'::jsonb, '["hervpod.com"]'::jsonb, '{}'::jsonb, '{"fdaStatus":"Registered with the FDA as an over-the-counter medical product, per hervpod.com. FDA registration means the company and product are listed with the FDA; it is not FDA clearance or approval.","materials":"Each pod is 3 in long x 2.5 in wide, with a 100% medical-grade silicone exterior and a flexible gel interior (the gel itself isn''t disclosed). Hypoallergenic, odor-free, and sterile when packaged. Made in China for Cool Comforts Co. (Cincinnati, OH).","recalls":"No recalls are mentioned on hervpod.com; check current FDA and manufacturer recall notices.","sideEffects":"Cold can feel too intense on sensitive skin, so VPod says to test the temperature first and limit each use to 20 minutes. Full warnings are listed below.","opinionAlerts":"hervpod.com contradicts itself on reuse: the product page says single-use and \"Do not reuse,\" but its FAQ and full instructions say the pod is reusable for up to 30 days with cleaning. ayna follows the detailed instructions; check the package insert."}'::jsonb, 'Cold therapy is a standard, low-risk way to ease vulvar and perineal soreness: ACOG recommends an ice pack or cold gel pack on the perineal area for 10 to 20 minutes at a time after birth, and a Cochrane review found cooling may reduce perineal pain in the first days postpartum (low-certainty evidence). VPod packages that idea as a curved silicone pod that stays in place in underwear.

Cooling only eases symptoms. It doesn''t treat yeast infections, BV, allergies, or menopause-related dryness, so it should be used alongside the right treatment, not instead of it. See a doctor for itching or burning that doesn''t go away, unusual discharge, or odor. VPod says it was developed with gynecologists; no study of VPod itself was found.', 'No customer reviews are shown on hervpod.com for this pack, and ayna didn’t find a retailer listing for the Elite single.', 'Cold therapy has category-level support for easing perineal pain (Cochrane; ACOG). No independent study of VPod was found, and cooling relieves symptoms only, not their underlying cause.', 'independent', 'ayna synthesis of ACOG guidance and a Cochrane review; not a direct clinician quote. Product details are from hervpod.com.', 'curated', false, false, null, true, '{"faqUrl":"https://hervpod.com/pages/faq","doctorOpinionShort":"Cold packs are an ACOG-recommended way to ease perineal soreness, and a Cochrane review found cooling may reduce postpartum perineal pain. VPod relieves symptoms but doesn''t treat their cause. No study of VPod itself was found.","whoItsFor":["Prepartum and postpartum soreness, including perineal tears, episiotomy, bruising, and swelling","Menopause-related vulvar discomfort","Anyone wanting an extra-soft pod for very tender areas"],"howToUse":{"intro":"Per VPod''s full instructions:","steps":["Put the unopened foil pack in the freezer for at least 1 hour, until the pod feels stiff.","Take it out and let it rest 3 to 5 minutes, then wash your hands and open the pack.","Touch the pod gently to your vulva first to check the temperature is comfortable.","Place it between the inner and outer labia (labia minora and majora), or in the center crotch of your underwear.","Wear it for up to 20 minutes, up to 3 times a day, waiting at least 10 minutes between uses.","After each use, rinse with warm water, wash with mild soap, and air dry; wipe with 70% isopropyl alcohol at least daily. Replace the pod after 30 days or if damaged."],"sourceUrl":"https://hervpod.com/pages/usage-instructions","sourceLabel":"hervpod.com: Instructions for Use"},"warnings":["External use only. Do not insert into the vagina or anus, and do not ingest.","For temporary symptom relief only; it does not treat yeast infections, BV, or other conditions. See a doctor for itching or burning that doesn’t go away, unusual discharge, or odor.","Remove before urinating, and don’t flush it.","Don’t use with other silicone-based products.","If the pod ruptures, clean the skin and throw the pod away (the gel may be slippery)."],"ingredients":"Medical-grade silicone exterior with a gel interior (gel not disclosed). Drug-free; no active ingredients.","scientificCitations":[{"url":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8094618/","text":"Local cooling for relieving pain from perineal trauma sustained during childbirth (Cochrane review, 2020)","summary":"A Cochrane review of 10 randomized trials (1,233 women) found that cooling with an ice pack or cold gel pad may reduce perineal pain in the first two days after birth, but the evidence is low to very low certainty. This is evidence for cold therapy in general, not for VPod specifically."},{"url":"https://www.acog.org/womens-health/faqs/postpartum-pain-management","text":"ACOG: Postpartum Pain Management","summary":"ACOG recommends applying an ice pack or cold gel pack to the perineal area for 10 to 20 minutes at a time to relieve discomfort after birth. This is clinical guidance for cold therapy as a category, not validation of a specific product."},{"url":"https://www.acog.org/womens-health/faqs/vulvovaginal-health","text":"ACOG: Vulvovaginal Health","summary":"ACOG suggests cold packs for perineal pain and advises seeing an ob-gyn for itching, burning, or swelling that doesn’t go away, since yeast infections, BV, and other causes need their own treatment. Cooling eases symptoms but doesn’t treat the cause."}],"verificationLinks":{"doctor":{"links":[]},"scientific":{"links":[]},"community":{"links":[{"platform":"website","url":"https://hervpod.com/products/vpod-elite-single-pack","text":"hervpod.com: VPod Postpartum & Menopause Comfort Single Pack","summary":"VPod’s own product page."}]}},"integrations":[],"badges":[],"isEmergingBrand":false}'::jsonb),
  ('p-vpod-elite-3-pack', 'VPod Postpartum & Menopause Comfort 3 Pack', 'VPod', 'postpartum', 'physical', 'VPod’s extra-soft cooling gel pod designed for new moms, for targeted relief of tearing, bruising, swelling, dryness, and irritation before and after birth, and for menopause-related discomfort. Like the Everyday pod, you freeze it and place it in your underwear for up to 20 minutes; it has a 100% medical-grade silicone exterior and is drug-free. It eases symptoms but doesn’t treat their cause. Three pods per pack; sold as VPod Elite.', '$55.99 (3 pods)', '/products/vpod/elite-3-pack.webp', 'https://hervpod.com/products/vpod-elite-multi-pack', '["discomfort","comfort","postpartum","pregnancy","menopause","external-only","reusable","hormone-free","cost"]'::jsonb, '["vaginal-health","comfort"]'::jsonb, '["hervpod.com","Walmart"]'::jsonb, '{}'::jsonb, '{"fdaStatus":"Registered with the FDA as an over-the-counter medical product, per hervpod.com. FDA registration means the company and product are listed with the FDA; it is not FDA clearance or approval.","materials":"Each pod is 3 in long x 2.5 in wide, with a 100% medical-grade silicone exterior and a flexible gel interior (the gel itself isn''t disclosed). Hypoallergenic, odor-free, and sterile when packaged. Made in China for Cool Comforts Co. (Cincinnati, OH).","recalls":"No recalls are mentioned on hervpod.com; check current FDA and manufacturer recall notices.","sideEffects":"Cold can feel too intense on sensitive skin, so VPod says to test the temperature first and limit each use to 20 minutes. Full warnings are listed below.","opinionAlerts":"hervpod.com contradicts itself on reuse: the product page says single-use and \"Do not reuse,\" but its FAQ and full instructions say the pod is reusable for up to 30 days with cleaning. ayna follows the detailed instructions; check the package insert."}'::jsonb, 'Cold therapy is a standard, low-risk way to ease vulvar and perineal soreness: ACOG recommends an ice pack